 "note": "What Vesuvius Radar collects and how it scores. scanner.py reads this file at every check. Keyword score: a scroll term adds the core weight; in each topic a strong term counts on its own and a weak term counts half, only when a context term (3D, CT, volume and the like) is also present; each negative term takes 15 off. Meaning score: the cosine similarity of the item's text to the anchor sentences below, from a small sentence-embedding model, mapped from [sim_floor, sim_ceiling] to 0..100. The final score is the higher of the keyword score and the blend (blend times the meaning score plus the rest times the keyword score), so meaning alone can lift an item to medium but not to high. Anchors and meaning searches are embedded as queries (query_prefix), items as passages.",
